From bae447ac275e214933a8326dce485361035b8c7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 12:36:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(images): 43 new slots, section-level paper figures, and
 motion that never crops a diagram
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The audit in docs/visual/IMAGE_BRIEF.md found 43 explanations with no picture.
All 43 arrived plus a corrected framework-hero, taking the site from 31 image
slots to 74.

Six of them are the service pages, which had no images at all — the six pages a
buyer lands on from a commercial search were the least illustrated on the site.
Twelve are paper figures placed at section level: the three papers had 21
sections and three figures between them, one hero each, while twelve of those
sections carried a table or a numbered sequence with nothing to look at. A
figure now sits beside the paragraph it explains.

The artwork was checked before it was wired. framework-hero carries the six
pillar names exactly as framework.ts spells them, with no date stamp.
fig-species-janka prints the published Janka values in the published order.
Twelve slots specified as flat vector came back flat, on-palette, with no text.
Nothing invented a figure the site does not publish. Every file is 1600px on the
long edge and under 90 KB/megapixel — 2.50 MB for all 44.

On the two sets: four archives arrived covering the same 44 ids, described as
different versions to rotate in the UI. They are not different versions.
Downscaled to identical dimensions and compared pixel-for-pixel the worst pair
differs by 3.16/255 — resampling noise; part1/part2 is 01/02 upscaled. So the
rotation was not built. Crossfading an image with a softer copy of itself is not
an effect, it reads as a rendering fault, and it doubles the bytes to do it.

Motion shipped instead. A scroll-in reveal on every figure, pure CSS behind
@supports so a browser without animation-timeline renders it normally rather
than blank. Ken Burns on exactly eight images — two heroes, six service photos —
and never on an explanatory figure, because scaling inside a fixed frame crops,
and a drifting axis label or a species leaving frame defeats the picture.

Two guards were passing on incomplete knowledge. verify-images had never been
told where service slugs come from and called six live routes 404s; the first
fix used the wrong pattern for SERVICES' one-line shape and changed nothing.
Folds in the orphan check from the unlanded patch 66 — supersedes it, and
supersedes patch 69.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
